  "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(y+3)^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 2(0+3)^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 2(3)^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 2(9)-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 18-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ -3{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, there are no $x$-intercepts.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
